# Generated / bulk financial product data.
#
# Three test files read from the shards below. Ignoring them wholesale made 27 tests
# pass locally and fail in CI, so the handful of ledger/fragment files those tests
# actually open are force-added (`git add -f`) and stay tracked despite these patterns:
#
#   data/20260829-cma-01/{index_rows,product_review_ledger}.jsonl
#   data/20260829-cma-01/{source_documents,evidence_refs}.fragment.json
#   data/ddakrate_parking_account_latest_full_20260830/data/financial_products/
#     category_builds/20260829-parking-account-01/{index_rows.jsonl,
#     source_documents.fragment.json,evidence_refs.fragment.json}
#
# Product JSON under these shards is deliberately NOT tracked -- it duplicates
# data/financial_products/normalized/products/, which the tests read instead.
# Adding a new file under an ignored shard requires `git add -f` plus an entry here.
data/financial_products/raw/
data/financial_products/staging/
data/financial_products/work/
data/financial_products/rebuild/
data/naver_savings_output/
data/financial_product_model_examples/
data/20260829-cma-01/
data/20260829-time-deposit-01-source-first-final/
data/ddakrate_installment_savings_shard_v015_20260831/
data/ddakrate_parking_account_latest_full_20260830/
# normalized/ is a runtime dependency (normalized_loader.py joins institution
# names through it), so it is tracked; only the build inputs are ignored.
data/institutions/raw/
data/institutions/staging/
data/multi_product_catalog/
